    "sio": "The world selector wraps0..12 and indexes13 world-name and logo-ID entries. Thirteen32-byte native SioWorldEntry records end at the independently referenced12-entry cursor-offset table; difficulty selection uses1..11 plus the physical zero entry. The13x12 card-position region contains12 navigation slots and its native zero terminator record. This entire change-card mode and table are genuinely absent in EU: its old absolute gUnk_09EF150C alias incorrectly coincided with gWorldNames. No EU definition or bytes are fabricated. All C placements retain their actual regional extents and opaque resource pointers remain assets.",
    "world_intro": "Won intro loops10 sprites and wraps its affine-frame index0..19, proving two10-record layouts and20 scales. The Agr schedule has19 live records plus its native final zero record before the next TaskDesc. TtMotion retains its canonical two6-element arrays, including unused stored values. The line task allocates33 entries; the physical33x3 halfword table includes31 live tuples, one extra stored tuple and a final zero tuple. It ends before two separate zero alignment bytes. Bks creates every explicit object ID0..13, proving the14-entry sprite, coordinate and timing arrays; its palette cycle uses entries1..6 of the two7-byte sequences. Array-tail alignment bytes remain outside the owned C extents."
